# {{TITLE}}

A contract-first Rust API generated by Minco {{MINCO_VERSION}}.

## Start

```bash
cp .env.example .env
set -a
source .env
set +a
cargo minco doctor
cargo minco config check
cargo minco contract sync --check
cargo minco check --with-cargo
{{DATABASE_SETUP}}
cargo minco db plan --set {{PACKAGE}}-{{DATABASE}} --json \
  > target/minco/migration-plan.json
MINCO_REVIEWED_MIGRATION_DIGEST="$(
  python3 -c 'import json; print(json.load(open("target/minco/migration-plan.json"))["digest"])'
)"
cargo minco db migrate \
  --set {{PACKAGE}}-{{DATABASE}} \
  --database-url-env DATABASE_MIGRATION_URL \
  --expected-plan-digest "$MINCO_REVIEWED_MIGRATION_DIGEST" \
  --receipt target/minco/migration-receipt.json
cargo run -p {{PACKAGE}}-service --bin {{PACKAGE}}-local
```

The API listens at `http://127.0.0.1:3000` by default.

## Architecture

```text
HTTP delivery -> application -> domain
adapters ---------------------> application ports (as features are added)
composition -> delivery + application + adapters
```

The OpenAPI document in `openapi/openapi.yaml` is authoritative. Do not edit
`crates/api/src/generated.rs` manually. Migration lifecycle metadata lives in
`{{MIGRATION_DIR}}/.minco-migrations.toml`; do not edit an applied SQL file to
change metadata.

## JJ workflow

This repository is initialized as a colocated JJ/Git repository unless `cargo minco new` was run with `--vcs none`.

```bash
jj status
jj workspace add ../{{PACKAGE}}-M0-T01 --name M0-T01
```
